  "statements": [
    {
      "type": "General Statements: All Other Content",
      "notes": "Often referred to as indian ginseng, Ashwagandha is noted for its ability to fortify adrenal function, energy and stress levels and is not a cardiac stimulant."
    },
    {
      "type": "General Statements: All Other Content",
      "notes": "Ashwagandha translates to scent of a horse, alluding to the power and strength it bestows. It was considered chief among the rasayana or rejuvenative herbs now called adaptogens."
    },
    {
      "type": "General Statements: All Other Content",
      "notes": "Featured Herb On Front: Ashwagandha (aerial parts)"
    },
    {
